{"type":"message","id":"c822f776","parentId":"156131af","timestamp":"2026-06-01T04:45:48.006Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API is accessible for reads but /send is returning 1101. This error code suggests a Cloudflare Workers limitation - error 1101 is \"Worker Exception\" which means the Worker itself is throwing an exception when trying to handle the /send request.\n\nThis is likely a bug in the ECHO platform's backend code, not a client-side issue. The platform is running but the /send endpoint is throwing an exception internally.\n\nLet me try a few more approaches to narrow down the issue.","thinkingSignature":"26d894b385924de888760c60e2aeac244e8cb91e55d252a15af1ce3edadb0c7b"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_v8ibegs8udj1_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat 04:45 UTC\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":200,"output":197,"cacheRead":22624,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23021,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780289144512,"responseId":"066c4179847fda121ea9f750512e67a2"}}
